{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793048965,"nonce":"6ahhbZvUeGsU+fWbHxl0G4JZNzk=","title":"Stabilize native SIGTRAP failures in exception, coroutine and filesystem conformance","message":"The final corpus after f4e866be reports native SIGTRAP crashes outside registered JIT code in Issue12213, TestCoroutines and TestFileSystem. Repeat probes reproduce all three in the saved immediate-parent 57f74b53 release, with RAYZOR_STD_PATH explicitly set to compiler/haxe-std. These must not be misclassified as new branch-typing regressions, but still block a reliable conformance gate.\n\nIssue12213 constructs/catches NotImplementedException and updates its stack: one crash among twelve parent launches. TestCoroutines: two successful parent launches followed by SIGTRAP. TestFileSystem: SIGTRAP on its first parent repeat. The native signal fault address is 0x000000018704e9f8 in these runs; callers differ by ASLR. The shared address alone does not establish one root cause.\n\nReports: /tmp/rayzor-conformance-throw-switch-final/report.tsv and logs/*.log; parent artifacts: /tmp/rayzor-issue12213-57f-repeat.json and /tmp/rayzor-testfilesystem-57f-repeat.json. Repeat command: saved-parent run --release --no-cache --preset application \u003centry from the case rayzor.toml\u003e, from the corresponding generated case directory. TestFileSystem lives under run/TestFileSystem/sys.\n\nRelated local-write loss and Issue11466 instability is tracked by 1d8027cf41c5b563c2d8e76b82bebfc92523b83dbdf2d541ddda1341e601d80c. Acceptance: repeated cold launches preserve values and exception/coroutine state without native crashes, and both full conformance and focused regressions remain stable under bounded parallel execution.","files":null}]}